1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,095
This YouTube channel was built by an
artificial intelligence, from a single

2
00:00:04,115 --> 00:00:04,479
prompt.

3
00:00:04,499 --> 00:00:09,322
The name, the logo, the banner, the
editing programs, and even this voice.

4
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:11,463
In this video, I'll show you that prompt,
block by block.

5
00:00:11,482 --> 00:00:14,346
The three mistakes the AI made.

6
00:00:14,366 --> 00:00:15,485
And how I fixed them.

7
00:00:15,505 --> 00:00:18,650
At the end, I'll give you the fixed
version, for free.

8
00:00:18,670 --> 00:00:23,368
It all started with a one-page text that I
pasted into Claude, Anthropic's assistant,

9
00:00:23,388 --> 00:00:24,700
connected to my browser.

10
00:00:24,720 --> 00:00:29,672
After that, I only did three things:
answer its questions, type my passwords,

11
00:00:29,692 --> 00:00:30,835
and say yes or no.

12
00:00:30,855 --> 00:00:32,668
Everything else was the AI.

13
00:00:32,688 --> 00:00:38,008
In one afternoon: the channel, its visual
identity, a code repository, and programs

14
00:00:38,028 --> 00:00:40,260
that edit the videos automatically.

15
00:00:40,280 --> 00:00:41,755
The prompt starts with a role.

16
00:00:41,775 --> 00:00:43,549
You are the producer of my channel.

17
00:00:43,569 --> 00:00:45,910
You do the work, I make the decisions.

18
00:00:45,930 --> 00:00:47,662
That sentence changes everything.

19
00:00:47,682 --> 00:00:49,789
The AI stops giving you advice.

20
00:00:49,809 --> 00:00:50,950
It takes action.

21
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:55,967
Next, you describe the channel: the theme,
the languages, the audience, and above all

22
00:00:55,987 --> 00:00:57,974
what viewers get from every video.

23
00:00:57,994 --> 00:00:59,161
Then the kick-off.

24
00:00:59,181 --> 00:01:03,492
The AI asks all its questions at once, and
proposes three names with a checked

25
00:01:03,512 --> 00:01:03,881
handle.

26
00:01:03,901 --> 00:01:05,067
Checked matters.

27
00:01:05,087 --> 00:01:07,417
For us, nine handles were already taken.

28
00:01:07,437 --> 00:01:10,290
Tempo News, Daily Brief, and seven more.

29
00:01:10,310 --> 00:01:14,800
The AI tested them one by one in YouTube
Studio, until it found a free name.

30
00:01:14,820 --> 00:01:16,593
The access block sets the limits.

31
00:01:16,613 --> 00:01:18,649
The AI does everything in the browser.

32
00:01:18,669 --> 00:01:20,893
But it only asks me for passwords.

33
00:01:20,913 --> 00:01:24,433
And it never deletes anything, or spends
money, without my approval.

34
00:01:24,453 --> 00:01:25,730
That's your seatbelt.

35
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:27,339
Up to that point, everything went well.

36
00:01:27,359 --> 00:01:29,468
Then the AI produced its first video.

37
00:01:29,488 --> 00:01:31,514
And three things went wrong.

38
00:01:31,534 --> 00:01:33,185
One: it picked the topic on its own.

39
00:01:33,205 --> 00:01:37,433
Anthropic going public, the company that
created it.

40
00:01:37,453 --> 00:01:39,205
That wasn't what I wanted.

41
00:01:39,225 --> 00:01:40,361
Fix, rule number one: topic first.

42
00:01:40,381 --> 00:01:44,950
The AI proposes three topics scored out of
ten, and produces nothing before my

43
00:01:44,970 --> 00:01:45,480
approval.

44
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,586
Two: for the visuals, it used drone shots
of New York.

45
00:01:48,606 --> 00:01:50,009
Nothing to do with the story.

46
00:01:50,029 --> 00:01:53,659
Fix, rule number two: every shot shows
what the sentence says.

47
00:01:53,679 --> 00:01:58,698
And only visuals we have the rights to:
screen captures, animations, credited free

48
00:01:58,718 --> 00:01:59,190
sources.

49
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:01,116
Three, and this one is the funniest.

50
00:02:01,136 --> 00:02:05,227
For the voice, it sent a style instruction
to the text-to-speech tool.

51
00:02:05,247 --> 00:02:06,920
Listen to the result.

52
00:02:06,940 --> 00:02:12,671
[in French] Read this text like a TV news
anchor: deep, calm, articulate voice,

53
00:02:12,691 --> 00:02:16,020
brisk but natural pace, no excessive
emphasis.

54
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:19,253
The voice read the instruction out loud.

55
00:02:19,273 --> 00:02:21,539
In all twelve audio files.

56
00:02:21,559 --> 00:02:24,724
And the AI didn't notice.

57
00:02:24,744 --> 00:02:28,271
Fix, rule number three: send only the
words to read, then transcribe every file

58
00:02:28,291 --> 00:02:28,810
to check it.

59
00:02:28,830 --> 00:02:31,150
Today, that check runs on every video.

60
00:02:31,170 --> 00:02:32,682
I added three more rules.

61
00:02:32,702 --> 00:02:34,290
Every number has a source.

62
00:02:34,310 --> 00:02:37,942
Every video brings something new, because
YouTube doesn't monetize mass-produced,

63
00:02:37,962 --> 00:02:38,799
repetitive content.

64
00:02:38,819 --> 00:02:41,860
And the description says which AI tools
were used.

65
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:46,282
The end of the prompt describes
production, step by step, from the script

66
00:02:46,302 --> 00:02:47,130
to the Shorts.

67
00:02:47,150 --> 00:02:51,144
Then approval: nothing gets published
without my okay.

68
00:02:51,164 --> 00:02:54,130
And every week, a report: views,
subscribers, costs and revenue.

69
00:02:54,150 --> 00:02:56,514
That's the master prompt, version two.

70
00:02:56,534 --> 00:03:01,106
It's free, in English and French, in the
description.

71
00:03:01,126 --> 00:03:03,050
Replace what's in brackets with your
theme, paste it into your AI, and watch it

72
00:03:03,070 --> 00:03:03,173
work.

73
00:03:03,193 --> 00:03:06,834
On this channel, I'm building a real
YouTube channel with AI, brick by brick,

74
00:03:06,854 --> 00:03:08,404
and showing you the real numbers.

75
00:03:08,424 --> 00:03:11,438
Next video: how AI finds topics that work.

76
00:03:11,458 --> 00:03:13,440
Subscribe so you don't miss it.
